**FUNCTION DESIGN**

| Component | Design |
|-----------|--------|
| Trigger | S3 upload (images/) |
| Input | Image file from S3 |
| Processing | Resize to thumbnail + medium |
| Output | Store in S3 (processed/) |

**IMPLEMENTATION**

```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const sharp = require('sharp');

const s3 = new AWS.S3();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const bucket = event.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;
  const key = decodeURIComponent(event.Records[0].s3.object.key.replace(/\+/g, ' '));

  // Get original image
  const image = await s3.getObject({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key }).promise();

  // Resize to thumbnail (150x150)
  const thumbnail = await sharp(image.Body)
    .resize(150, 150)
    .toBuffer();

  // Resize to medium (800x800)
  const medium = await sharp(image.Body)
    .resize(800, 800)
    .toBuffer();

  // Upload processed images
  await Promise.all([
    s3.putObject({
      Bucket: bucket,
      Key: `processed/thumbnails/${key}`,
      Body: thumbnail,
      ContentType: 'image/jpeg'
    }).promise(),
    s3.putObject({
      Bucket: bucket,
      Key: `processed/medium/${key}`,
      Body: medium,
      ContentType: 'image/jpeg'
    }).promise()
  ]);

  return { statusCode: 200 };
};
```

**CONFIGURATION**

| Setting | Value | Reason |
|---------|-------|--------|
| Memory | 1024 MB | Image processing needs memory |
| Timeout | 30 seconds | Processing can take time |
| Runtime | Node.js 18 | Current LTS |
| Layers | Sharp layer | Pre-compiled binary |

